// Page Intro Text :
"P1335893365" "{HeroName}. Take this. You'll find the entrance in the sewers.<br><br><color orange>Santiago hands you a slip of paper with directions scribbled on its back. At the very bottom it reads, 'good until next week'. These must be directions to get into the underground base of the Resistance.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P784713589" "What's up, slammer?! Old top-hat sent you over here to mish-mash with me, huh?! Well I'm all down for that!<br><br>I think you and me, we're gonna be banging on some portraits and tearing up the screens all over this place!"
// Answer Text :
"P1864933015" "... what?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1484189843" "Have you heard of <color yellow>Ricochet</color>?<br><br>She's one of the finest members of the Resistance, always willing to take the good fight to Cole and his dogs.<br><br>If you really want to give us a hand on the frontlines, you should speak with Ricochet. I can give you her current coordinates.<br><br><color orange>Ricochet is the first contact in the Crusader storyline for the Resistance. Crusaders are ruthless members of the Resistance who are willing to do whatever it takes to bring down Cole. Some whisper that certain members of the Crusaders don't even care about the goals of the Resistance - they just enjoy creating chaos.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P104663558" "Meet with Ricochet"
// SendOffString :
"P2232231058" "Alright, it's not going to be exactly <i>easy</i> to get to Ricochet. She's in one of our <color yellow>underground bases</color> within Nova.<br><br>We have a shortcut that you can take through the tunnels. Speak to a man named Santiago - he will help you get down into our base."

